{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact installed-registers head c0a94ebfde28305d2e4c55a36df58aff45862bb8 on builder/installed-registers-20261103, tree 15597483, for request 579489e0 under promise 95f5bc73 and review request de1e49cc. This approval covers INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES, child admission under listed registers, health and the operator instructions. It claims no deployment, no H3 check and no G3 acceptance.\n\nScope. Main 6a67cc08 is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. Against main, the head changes five scope sources, three tests, the security inventory test, docs/deploy.md, docs/security/settings.md, the design, the note and three manifests. The commit-message check passes for all six commits. No card or Page path changes. From the gate commit 8cdd44cd to the head, only notes change.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- readInstalledRegisters accepts the setting only beside a pinned current register. The value must be a strict JSON array of at most 4,096 bytes, with 1 to 32 distinct scope IDs that include the current register. Anything else reads as misconfigured, which closes child creation and makes health unavailable. Without the setting, the list is the current register alone, as before.\n- parentlessCreationAdmission still admits only the current register's own install. A listed old register cannot found a new root.\n- admitChildCreation changes one comparison: the lineage root must now appear in the operator's list instead of equaling the current register. Every other check stays: signatures, incarnation, applied genesis, source send, cohort, index, bytes, visits and deadline. The index must already know the root.\n- The scope-index adapter keys its cached policy on the raw setting string, so a changed list replaces the policy.\n- Health still probes only the current register. A misconfigured list reads as unavailable.\n- Control 07 restores single-register equality, and the old-root case fails. Control 08 admits every checked root, and the unlisted case fails. Both name baseline 0a0bc465…, the exact creation-lineage.ts at the head, and both restore it.\n\nThe local Worker scene ran over real HTTP with persistent storage. After the switch to the new current register, the old room's Inbox and lane both show decision applied, with exact hashes and genesis under the old room. A third root that the switched list omits accepted a genuine join, but its Inbox delivery answered not-found three times and ended undelivered, and the child read answers not-found. The note keeps the two inspection mistakes on the record, and read-only reads repair them without repeating any Native act.\n\nThe gate passed. gate.exit at 8cdd44cd reads exit 0. source-before and source-after both record tree fa3e9257 and a clean status, and every stage passed with no unhandled error. The gate covers the landed registration-recovery source too. After the witness checkpoint c3995f85, only that merge changes source, and creation-lineage.ts is unchanged.\n\nEvidence. The three manifests hash to a70e685c…, 77391950… and 518830e6…, and the note names all three. All 47 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, every SHA256SUMS file matches, and no unit holds an unlisted file. All 525 private files match their indexes. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The operator's configuration decides which roots may have children, and Native lineage still proves each birth. No request or index row can add a root.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The list widens admission only to roots an operator records, and each one still needs its own checked Native birth on that Worker.\n\nSimplification: no required change. One note for deployments: removing a register from the list stops child creation in every room under it. docs/deploy.md requires a record of the affected rooms before removal. The planner's receipts should name the configuration commit for each list change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fa36a2ac0d3a69e3ed72d3deba78f7aa532b8665","binding":"assigned","head":"c0a94ebfde28305d2e4c55a36df58aff45862bb8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4d525cf4b82505a4f23aefbddb2ab8fc0e7bbfbf\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:eed841315c8f947e75113b06cabe3756cd07b1ff\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:95f5bc739f9ba74c86be195f8a96fb52fa989307\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2a3ea3a1018ce5e5bb94e3211c4970d22246ba02","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}